    <string name="title_usage">How to Use</string>
    <string name="usage_text">API Key is used to check account balance. Create or copy one at platform.deepseek.com/api_keys.\n\nUser Token is used to query daily usage details. Log in to platform.deepseek.com, open browser developer tools, and run the following in the Console:\n\nlocalStorage.getItem(\'userToken\')\n\nCopy the returned value and paste it into the input field above.</string>
    <string name="usage_text_multi">Tap \"Add\" to connect multiple LLM providers:\n\n· DeepSeek Official: enter an API Key to check balance; optionally enter a User Token (run localStorage.getItem(\'userToken\') in the browser Console after logging into platform.deepseek.com) to fetch daily usage details.\n\n· OpenAI Compatible / Relay: enter any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Relays built on New-API / One-API will automatically expose token balance; OpenAI official accounts will try the subscription quota API. If a provider has no balance API, the balance shows 0 and you can still view trends in Analytics.\n\n· Switch between providers at the top of the Chat tab.</string>
